<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/20th-century">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · Treaty</p><h1 class="enc-title">Treaty of Fez</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1912">1912</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Treaty of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/fez">Fez</a> was signed on 30 March 1912 by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sultan">Sultan</a> <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/abd-al-hafid-of-morocco">Abd al-Hafid of Morocco</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/france">France</a> after the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/agadir-crisis">Agadir Crisis</a>. It made <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/morocco">Morocco</a> a French <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/protectorate">protectorate</a>, with a resident-general holding real power while the sultan and his makhzen government were kept in place. A Franco-Spanish agreement later that year gave <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/spain">Spain</a> a protectorate in the north. The treaty remained in force until Moroccan independence in 1956.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/treaty-of-fez.jpg" alt="Treaty of Fez" width="320" height="484" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Ministère de l'Europe et des Affaires étrangères · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Trait%C3%A9_relatif_%C3%A0_l%27organisation_du_protectorat_fran%C3%A7ais_dans_l%27empire_ch%C3%A9rifien_TRA19120019_001_-_France_Maroc.pdf" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
